duced or co-produced some 60 movies over the years and continued to be busy as a producer. He has produced most of the Olsen-banden movies and is the producer of Denmark most successful TV series Matador (1978–1982).\n\n", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-08-01T14:14:03.539726+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 1735, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bo_Christensen"}], "uuid": "06f7dc7b-e431-4a43-abab-61221b59cc8a", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "16038", "external_references": [{"id": 7567, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q3676033"}, {"id": 7568, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "117611853"}, {"id": 7569, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "no00023060"}, {"id": 7570, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-no00023060"}], "date_modified": "2023-08-01T14:14:03.551575+10:00"}, {"id": 76738, "name": "Just Betzer", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2106233, "title": "Babette's Feast = Babettes Gaestebud", "work_id": 80860, "role": "co-producer", "role_id": 915, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "1944-06-11", "date_of_death": "2003-11-06", "places_of_operation": [{"id": 34, "name": "Denmark", "slug": "denmark"}], "biography": "Just Betzer (11 June 1944 – 6 November 2003), was a Danish Oscar-winning film producer, born in Åbyhøj, Denmark.Betzer began his career managing the candy concession and as an alternate projectionist at his father's theater in Aarhus, Denmark, in 1955. In 1960, Betzer founded Panorama Film production/distribution company in Denmark, which has since made over 30 feature films. He later opened a chain of 13 theatres throughout Denmark. In 1985, Betzer moved to England, and started the London-based company Panorama Film International with offices in Copenhagen, Denmark and Los Angeles, California.\nIn 1987, the film Babette's Feast, produced by Betzer, was released.  Babette's Feast won the Academy Award for Best Foreign-Language Film, and the BAFTA Best Foreign Film award, in 1988. Two years later, he opened the Los Angeles-based production company, Just Betzer Films. His other films include Winterborn, Assassination, And You Thought Your Parents Were Weird, Nobody's Perfect, The Misfit Brigade, and the erotic The Girl in a Swing, with Meg Tilly. Betzer died from a coronary embolism at age 59 on 6 November 2003, in Lumsaas, Denmark.", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-08-01T15:45:38.748698+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 2495, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Just_Betzer"}], "uuid": "275119dd-35e1-4024-819e-cc633e56beef", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "22938", "external_references": [{"id": 10672, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q6315877"}, {"id": 10673, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "91967053"}, {"id": 10674, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "no97011706"}, {"id": 10675, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-no97011706"}], "date_modified": "2023-08-01T15:45:38.762089+10:00"}, {"id": 76737, "name": "Michel Choquet", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 899971, "title": "Le Chant du Monde", "work_id": 80851, "role": "co-producer", "role_id": 915, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "1936-09-13", "date_of_death": null, "places_of_operation": [{"id": 17, "name": "France", "slug": "france"}], "biography": "", "biography_author": null, "date_of_biography": null, "external_links": [], "uuid": "c7e7ded3-44b4-4362-ba32-db7639e986f5", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": null, "external_references": [{"id": 11648, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q3309243"}, {"id": 11649, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "260120717"}, {"id": 11650, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "no2012112820"}, {"id": 11651, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-no2012112820"}], "date_modified": "2023-06-14T16:33:30.576250+10:00"}, {"id": 76736, "name": "Claire Duval", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 899970, "title": "Le Chant du Monde", "work_id": 80851, "role": "co-producer", "role_id": 915, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": null, "date_of_death": null, "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "", "biography_author": null, "date_of_biography": null, "external_links": [], "uuid": "89f98017-767c-4ab3-a8f1-392ed7ecc2f5", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": null, "external_references": [], "date_modified": "2023-06-14T16:33:30.576250+10:00"}, {"id": 76735, "name": "Cliff Reid", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2356119, "title": "The Informer", "work_id": 80838, "role": "producer", "role_id": 1089, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2097694, "title": "Annie Oakley", "work_id": 81309, "role": "producer", "role_id": 1089, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "1891-09-07", "date_of_death": "1959-08-22", "places_of_operation": [{"id": 1, "name": "United States of America", "slug": "united-states-of-america"}], "biography": "Cliff Reid (September 7, 1891 – August 22, 1959), also known as George Clifford Reid, was an American film producer and film production studio founder during the 1930s and 1940s. In addition he also directed film shorts, and was the assistant director on several feature films.", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-08-01T14:29:32.247828+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 3793, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cliff_Reid"}], "uuid": "761fbf73-f9ef-4b78-8a4c-40cbfb3d5623", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "17118", "external_references": [{"id": 26810, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q20828223"}, {"id": 27912, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "117916737"}, {"id": 27913, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "n85273981"}, {"id": 27914, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-n85273981"}], "date_modified": "2023-08-01T14:29:32.270782+10:00"}, {"id": 76734, "name": "Maximilian Schell", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 1986919, "title": "Judgment at Nuremberg", "work_id": 83107, "role": "cast", "role_id": 33, "is_primary": false}, {"id": 1984826, "title": "Marlene", "work_id": 80834, "role": "director", "role_id": 938, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "1930-12-08", "date_of_death": "2014-02-01", "places_of_operation": [{"id": 26, "name": "Switzerland", "slug": "switzerland"}], "biography": "Maximilian Schell (8 December 1930 – 1 February 2014) was an Austrian-born Swiss film and stage actor, who also wrote, directed and produced some of his own films. He won the Academy Award for Best Actor for the 1961 American film Judgment at Nuremberg, his second acting role in Hollywood. Born in Austria, his parents were involved in the arts and he grew up surrounded by acting and literature. While he was a child, his family fled to Switzerland in 1938 when Austria was annexed by Nazi Germany, and they settled in Zurich. After World War II ended, Schell took up acting or directing full-time. He appeared in numerous German films, often anti-war, before moving on to Hollywood.\nSchell was top billed in a number of Nazi-era themed films, as he could speak both English and German. Among those were two films for which he received Oscar nominations: The Man in the Glass Booth (1975; best actor), where he played a character with two identities, and Julia (1977; best supporting actor), where he helps the underground in Nazi Germany.\nHis range of acting went beyond German characters, however; and during his career, he also played personalities as diverse as Venezuelan leader Simón Bolívar, Russian emperor Peter the Great, and physicist Albert Einstein. For his role as Vladimir Lenin in the television film Stalin (1992) he won the Golden Globe Award. On stage, Schell acted in a number of plays, and his was considered \"one of the greatest Hamlets ever.\"Schell was an accomplished pianist and conductor, performing with Claudio Abbado and Leonard Bernstein, and with orchestras in Berlin and Vienna. His elder sister, Maria Schell, was also an internationally noted actress, about whom he produced the documentary My Sister Maria, in 2002.", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2022-05-19T12:26:35.809558+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 2685, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximilian_Schell"}], "uuid": "64c4ac07-0a11-456f-94d7-227e22156070", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": null, "external_references": [{"id": 11459, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q153018"}, {"id": 11460, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "19866935"}, {"id": 11461, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "n86025468"}, {"id": 11462, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-n86025468"}], "date_modified": "2023-06-14T16:33:30.576250+10:00"}, {"id": 76733, "name": "Matthew Flanagan", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2356352, "title": "The Irish in Australia: Echo of a Distant Drum", "work_id": 80832, "role": "co-director", "role_id": 959, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 1805088, "title": "Heartlands with Dean Graetz : arid", "work_id": 86989, "role": "producer", "role_id": 1089, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 906307, "title": "Heartlands : taking control", "work_id": 86992, "role": "co-producer", "role_id": 915, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 906308, "title": "Heartlands : ta